AB  - This paper, on the basis of experimenting how various situations of exercises affect the SPA of 150 college students, yields the following results: physical exercises in all sports situations can positively reduce the SPA of students; the reduction of SPA in exercises of cognitive group is superior to those of non-cognitive individual; gender differences function in how cognition affects SPA; the cognition plays a vital role in the reduction of female SPA; the size of group has diverse effects on the reduction of male and female SPA, but this is not statistically significant.
