AB  - This note is about how the process of assessment worked, together with some reflections on the general implications for the two subjects covered here. As such, it represents the collective views of the Social Policy and Social Work Panel, not those of the UK Higher Education Funding Councils or the Research Assessment Exercise (RAE) team. Originally, that team ruled that there should be no feedback to individual institutions except in a strictly limited number of cases where formal written comments were being provided. However, just as we went to press this decision was modified. After sustained pressure (in which we played some part), it has been agreed that there can now be some informal feedback from chairs to individual institutions. We return to this important change of policy at the end of this article.
